{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792097529,"nonce":"J/kqblMg5FZtWOBFpDHkNBSQ2Fw=","message":"Revised 2026-10-15 (app.md A7): `expand` on list and gantt, `show` (the map Enter opens by), and show's own `fields` and `expand` all become one `shows={type: spec}` map, the spec being exactly what show takes less the id. A row nests by its type's spec, recursively, a cycle ending at an ancestor; `links` is skipped where a row nests. Spec resolution is whole, not merged: the call's shows[type], then the type's `show` in the schema, then {\"expand\":[\"links\"]}. Flows in flows/ and every test using expand or show change with it.","files":null}]}